We’re Hiring an Executive – Compliance

Job Title: Executive – Compliance
Experience: 1+ Year
Location: Pune
Employment Type: Full-Time
Notice Period: Immediate to 15 Days


Main Duties: 

Assisting for client onboarding / take-on and sign off exercise (including making pre-onboarding file reviews, as and when applicable); 
• Ensuring regular compliance follow up on the files and the effective implementation of reviews; 
• Overseeing the client’s compliance and reporting to the Head of Compliance / Manager; 
• Liaising with the regulatory bodies of different jurisdictions where the JurisTax Group operates; 
• Assisting in the pre-visit preparation and onsite visit of regulators; 
• Engaging actively in adoption and implementation of KYC principles and the anti-money laundering and combatting terrorism financing measures, laws and guidelines; 
• Assisting on the drafting and updating of Compliance and AML policies and procedures, regulatory returns and compliance reviews of company literature; 
• Conducting training sessions for educating and advising staff and senior management on compliance issues, coordinating personnel training requirements, identifying business risks and keeping up to date with changes to AML and Compliance regulatory requirements; 
• Updating the compliance library on an ongoing basis (constitutive documents, client acceptance forms, manuals, policies and Operations Manuals); 
• Assisting on TFS screening and reporting process; 
• Assisting in the Transaction Monitoring framework (including GoAML supervision); 
• Ability to understand and update our policies and manuals to the applicable AML-CFT framework of jurisdictions where the Group is present; 
• Maintaining all inhouse registers up to date; 
• Assist in providing AML / CFT and Compliance trainings (including setting of questions); 
• Preparation of dashboards and such other reporting (including preparation of Board and committee memos); 
• Searching for latest news in the field of corporate law, international financial sector and related industries; and 
• Any other related work/ assignment specific research as may be requested by the Reporting line. 

Qualifications: 
• Degree in Law/ Finance/ management or other related qualifications; 
• 1-2 years of experience in compliance or in the financial services industry; 
• Knowledge of industry processes and regulations; and 
• Good communication and interpersonal abilities. 


How to Apply:
Send your updated resume to info@nexio.in
